# Every text file is stored and checked out with LF line endings, whatever core.autocrlf
# says on the machine that clones the repository. eval/run.py records the sha256 of the
# code, prompt and scenario files in each run's run_meta.json. On a CRLF checkout (the Git
# for Windows default) every one of those hashes would differ, and the committed results
# would look as if they came from changed code.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary: stored byte for byte, never converted. One changed byte corrupts a gzip file
# (the vendored tokenizer, pilot/data/qwen3_tokenizer.json.gz) or a SQLite database.
*.gz binary
*.sqlite binary
